===Death ritual===
To Sunneists, a corpse is considered dirty and of no value to the gods or the living. As such, the corpses are left in roofless structures outside of towns called [[NAME]] to rot while exposed to [[Sunne]] and [[Mōna]], and left to the animals who feast on them. This [[wikipedia:excarnation|excarnation]] is then followed by the cremation of the remains to remove all impurities, a funeral rite known as [[NAME]].

===Sexuality===
In Sunneist doctrine, sexuality is a creation of the Divine Couple, like everything in the biological sphere. 

Sexuality is therefore essentially something good by nature: it is the natural path for procreation, and all the components of pleasure associated with sexuality, in particular the sexual pleasure associated with the act itself, form in principle a legitimate and desirable thing.
 
